  "body": "## What changed\n\nA setup can now hold the part aligned - flipped, turned, or as modelled - separate from its work offset (#326, part of #308).\n\n- **Storage:** `SetupDef.part_alignment: Option<Location>` - the rigid transform from the document frame into the setup frame. `None` = \"As modelled\" (never stored as identity). Only parts (models that are not fixtures) read through it; the setup's stock, work offsets and fixtures already live in the setup frame.\n- **Command:** `AlignPartToSetup` (undoable, validated at construction). `new(world, setup, Option<Location>)` takes any rigid transform (the door #330's picks will use); `preset(..)` (As modelled, Flip over X/Y, Turn 90/180/270 about Z) and `angles(.., [x, y, z]°)` turn the part about the centre of its bounds. Quarter turns use exact quaternion components.\n- **Stock follows** like it follows `MoveModel` (stock from a part, or a one-part document's stock): a box/cylinder is rebuilt square to the setup frame. A cylinder that would lie on its side, or a following stock shared with another setup, is refused by name. `MoveModel` moves an aligned setup's stock as that setup sees the move. A datum transfer (`CreateSetup` from a setup) carries the alignment.\n- **Work offset untouched.** `setup::wcs_slot` and the G-word come from the setup exactly as before (#331); rotated offsets stay refused at post (#315/#325).\n- **Generation / stock / sim / post in the setup frame:** op material, Top/Bottom of Model and source-selection heights, the program sim's part, Fit to Models / Fit sides, stock from model, the part-size readout, the viewport's part drawing and picks (active setup's frame).\n- **Stamps:** an entity source's pose is digested in the setup frame, and an aligned setup's alignment enters every op stamp of that setup. Nothing is written when as modelled, so no existing stamp moves.\n- **Project v53:** `setup.part_alignment {translation, rotation}`; absent = as modelled, so every v52 file loads unchanged; a non-rigid transform is refused as corrupt. Not breaking (nothing loadable before is refused).\n- **UI:** Setups page row \"Part alignment\" - a quick-choice combo plus typed X/Y/Z angles with Apply, queuing `CommandKind::AlignPart`.\n\n## Refused by name in an aligned setup (this slice)\n\nGeneration is wired and pinned for **Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive** over a whole model or the stock. Refused at `collect_job` (the one door every generation passes), so an aligned setup never cuts in the unaligned frame:\n- every other kind (3D, drilling, multi-axis, turning, ...);\n- picked faces/edges as the source; area controls; a 3+2 tilt;\n- any non-mill machine (lathe, mill-turn).\n\nThe program sim refuses a program spanning setups that hold the part differently (carrying cut stock between alignments is #317). An op generated before an alignment change is Stale and never posts.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Fixture: 40 x 40 x 20 block with a 20 x 20 hole blind to Z 10, stock 60 x 60 x 22 from Z -2, 4 mm end mill, whole-model Contour Z 20 -> 12.\n- As modelled the cut levels run the hole ring at 8 mm and the outer ring at 22 mm. Flipped over X (stored rotation exactly `[1, 0, 0, 0]`, translation `(0, 0, 20)` = about the part centre Z 10): only the outer ring at 22 mm - Z 12..20 is the former bottom, solid. Posts at G54.\n- The stock follows square: 60 x 60 x 22 now from Z 0 (the 2 mm under the part is 2 mm over it). A Turn 90 about Z lays a 60 x 40 block 40 x 60.\n- Flip then As modelled: the op is Ok again without regenerating, and the regenerated program is byte-identical.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/setup_align.rs` (new):\n- `as_modelled_is_byte_identical_and_the_stamp_returns_fresh`\n- `a_flipped_setup_contours_the_former_bottom_and_posts_in_its_frame`\n- `a_quarter_turn_rebuilds_the_stock_square_and_undo_redo_walk_it`\n- `two_setups_hold_the_part_differently_without_touching_each_other`\n- `unverified_kinds_and_picks_are_refused_by_name_in_an_aligned_setup`\n- `the_alignment_round_trips_and_older_files_load_as_modelled`\n- `the_program_sim_refuses_by_name_across_differently_held_setups`\n- `the_pocket_and_face_kinds_cut_the_flipped_part_and_post`\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_align_tests.rs` (new):\n- `the_alignment_control_turns_the_part_through_the_command`\n- `typed_angles_reach_the_same_command_and_a_refusal_says_why`\n\n## Gate (quick, debug, in the worktree)\n\n- camcraft-app suites green: setup_align 8, golden_cl 23, conformance 6, posting 17, project_roundtrip 68, commands_undo 32, setups 11, setup_wcs 7, rotated_wcs 4, setup_defines_wcs 4, heights 11, heights_selection 9, fixtures 14, pick 9, remachining 6, stock_play 7, setup_sheet 7, operations 117 (6 ignored, heavy lane).\n- camcraft-ui lib (CWD crates/ui): 291 passed, 2 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Goldens unchanged (as modelled is byte-identical).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/326-setup-part-alignment.md`. Found on the way: #340 (the loader does not pin a stock's geometry revision; side-stepped here).\n\nNot done here: picks writing the alignment (#330), the setup-to-setup transform (#316), the move gizmo and setup sheet still read the document pose.\n\nChangelog: Setups can hold the part flipped or turned (presets or typed angles), with the stock following square to the setup frame; Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive generate and post in that frame, every other kind is refused by name in an aligned setup. Project files go to v53 (older files load as modelled).\n\nFixes #326\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
